   232	
   233	### Vertical agents — the semantic standard (ratified 2026-08-08)
   234	
   235	**"Vertical agent" is the one product noun.** The earlier niche-agent /
   236	influencer-agent taxonomy is dissolved: an influencer agent is simply a
   237	vertical agent whose niche is a person or brand. Every vertical agent is the
   238	same shape — **fleet seat + persona/knowledge package + its own landing page**
   239	(`<agent>.senecaapp.ai`). This is the direct execution of VISION Horizon 1 and
   240	GTM Motions 5/2b.
   241	
   242	The surviving distinction is **AUDIENCE**, not agent kind:
   243	
   244	- **Private vertical agent** — invite-only members, hand-provisioned
   245	  workspace, workspace/BYOK funding. **Fully operational today** once the
   246	  landing validation queue merges.
   247	- **Public vertical agent** — open registration from the landing page →
   248	  per-signup workspace via the D28 signup-domain hook, pooled funding.
   249	  **REQUIRES** self-signup work, spend caps, and abuse guardrails before
   250	  opening.
   251	
   252	**Every agent launches private; "going public" is a per-hostname ops decision
   253	once caps exist.** The former "influencer agent" gap list in the snapshot is
   254	re-labeled **public-vertical-agent features** (self-signup, caps/guardrails,
   255	channels) — see [`state/2026-08-08.md`](state/2026-08-08.md) §5–6 with its
   256	errata.
   257	
   258	Sequencing consequences (ratified):
   259	
   260	- The niche-vs-influencer ordering dissolves: **ship landing pages per agent
   261	  now (private)**; pull self-signup only when the first public vertical agent
   262	  needs it. Wave 1.5 = merge the landing/default-agent validation queue, then
   263	  ship one named vertical agent end-to-end on a real hostname before further
   264	  Wave 3/4 expansion.
   265	- **#1107 slice 3 (workspace install/update path — add agents without
   266	  redeploy) is queued next** in the agent-packaging lane, below landing/BYOK.
   267	
   268	### Commercial premises (ratified 2026-08-08)
   269	
   270	- **boring-ui provides the PREMISES, never the pricing.** The platform ships
   271	  the capability substrate — per-user and per-workspace provider credentials
   272	  (the BYOK vault), provenance-labeled provider rows in the model picker
   273	  (workspace / personal / platform-credits), and, when a consumer pulls it, a
   274	  per-workspace usage-facts feed (#819). It stays commercially neutral and
   275	  must not preclude any pricing topology.
   276	- **Each app/tenant repo adapts the strategy for its segment** (Seneca first):
   277	  e.g. monthly subscription (with BYOK or included usage) for private B2B
   278	  vertical agents; credits for public-vertical-agent funnels when self-signup
   279	  opens. Billing systems live app-side; the platform only ever emits facts.
   280	- **Sequencing consequence:** #819 metering ships only when a usage-priced
   281	  offer pulls it — the platform emits facts, the app bills. It is NOT a
   282	  blocker for the first vertical agent under subscription pricing. This
   283	  amends the metering recommendation in
   284	  [`state/2026-08-08.md`](state/2026-08-08.md) §3/§4 (errata noted there).
   285	
   286	### Lane priorities (ratified 2026-08-08)
   287	
   288	- **#1123 executable environments: ACTIVE at LOW priority** — it is what
   289	  analyst vertical agents need to execute over client data. Background slices
   290	  continue; it never preempts landing, BYOK, or #1107.
